# A fixed defect, named after it (CLAUDE.md §9; Go's `test/fixedbugs`).
#
# SYMPTOM, 2026-09-02 (panel 102's compiler-engineer, on its way to something
# else; reproduced by the coordinator the same hour, and again 2026-09-03):
# this program was accepted by `heroes check` at exit 0, printed `2` and then
# `panic: 1 heap blocks still live at exit (a missing decref) — this is a
# compiler bug`, exit 134; with the second call it was exit 133 and no output;
# under `--sanitize` it was `AddressSanitizer: heap-use-after-free`, a READ of
# size 8 in `hero_array_decref`. `spec:88` forbids the program: *only a
# declared `@` name can be mutated*, and `b` is a parameter without `@`.
#
# CAUSE: the write half of an `@` argument was never checked. `write_root`,
# the resolver's rule for the left of `@`, had exactly one caller — the
# mutation STATEMENT — and the checker's `marker_mismatch` asked only whether
# the argument's marker matched the PARAMETER's marker, never whether the
# argument's root was a cell. So the callee copied out into a by-value copy
# the caller then released twice.
#
# FIX, 2026-09-03 (M-robustness-guards step 1): `resolve/writes.hero`'s
# `inout_root` holds the root of every `@` argument to the rule of the left
# of `@`. Eight shapes were measured before the repair and seven passed; the
# eight cases beside this one are those shapes, one each.
record Bag
    items: [str]

function add(@b: Bag, s: str)
    b.items @ b.items.push(s)

function reader(b: Bag)
    add(@b, "x")  #~ not_mutable
    add(@b, "y")  #~ not_mutable
    print(b.items.len())

function main()
    bag = Bag(items: ["a"])
    reader(bag)
    print(bag.items.len())

# Since 2026-09-10 the specification's sections are numbered and a citation names
# the section, never a line (CL-037). The line numbers above were written against
# the layout at commit 834d804f; read today they are:
#   spec:88 is spec § 5 Bindings` forbids the program: *only a
